Parses each argument of a compound expression once per level, so a nested
chain whose innermost call fails no longer takes time exponential in its
depth. An overload that takes the call's arity reports its own errors instead
of parsing the arguments again for a combined message, as maplibre-style-spec
does, and the legacy filter comparisons take a number or a string through one
signature instead of two overloads of the same arity
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1432).
Upstream: not proposed

